# Normalize line endings.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone under `core.autocrlf=true` gets a CRLF working
# tree against this repo's LF index. PHPCS then reports a wave of phantom
# Generic.Files.LineEndings.InvalidEOLChar errors that CI, running on Linux,
# never sees — sending you chasing ~37 findings that do not exist.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF too, so the platform and the local
# autocrlf setting stop mattering.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts CI executes must keep LF whatever the checkout does.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files: never normalize, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.svgz binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary
*.mo  binary
